ses of tens of billions  of tax cuts or at least intended tax  increases not going to  happen 100 billion or more on energy  further sums on spending and on tax cuts  you've probably already noticed a  pattern about trust anomics it's quite  expensive  so where's that money going to come from  trust will actually say borrowing is not  a constraint  bahrain is an option at the moment we  need to have fiscal discipline we need  to have financial support just borrow as  much as you want no it's about having  censored there  it's not borrowing as much as you want  it's about having a sense of economic  policy still it all points to higher  debt and the more debt they're racking  up over there in westminster the higher  all our sequel interest rates will go so  this place the bank of england becomes  all important as does  the wider city because if you are  borrowing money then you really need to  find someone to lend it to you  that in the end was why george osborne  and rishi sunak didn't do things like  this  if trustonomics works it could mean we  get through the current crisis and maybe  even get better off  if not well it could be a bumpy few  years  ed conway sky news
 

